=== (b)+(c) run-time bridge, real / (rc.conf has no bridge9, no cloned_interfaces)
  ok       network                            bridge9
                                                exists (members [epair0a vtnet1]); setup allow-lists it and changes nothing on it
  warn     network                            bridge9
                                                exists only at run time: rc.conf has no ifconfig_bridge9 line, so after a reboot it is gone (or comes back without its members) and guests on it lose their network
  manual   network                            bridge9 vlanfilter
                                                not set; changing an existing bridge can cut off its members, so setup prints the steps (each member's PVID first, then defuntagged, then vlanfilter); run them from the console. Without it the agent reports bridge_vlan_unfiltered. The rc.conf line leaves out [epair0a]: guest ports the agent creates when a guest starts
                                                $ ifconfig bridge9 ifuntagged epair0a 1
                                                $ ifconfig bridge9 ifuntagged vtnet1 1
                                                $ ifconfig bridge9 defuntagged 1
                                                $ ifconfig bridge9 vlanfilter
                                                $ sysrc cloned_interfaces+="bridge9"
                                                $ sysrc ifconfig_bridge9="addm vtnet1 ifuntagged vtnet1 1 defuntagged 1 vlanfilter up"
                                                      "bridge9"
                                                    ],
                                                    "management_interfaces": [
                                                      "vtnet0"
                                                    ]
                                                  }
                                                }

